## Commands

Bearer on every call. `{ok:false}` = stop.

| Method | Path | Body |
|--------|------|------|
| `POST` | `/v1/sessions` | `platform`, `files`, `public_key?`, `listen?` |
| `DELETE` | `/v1/sessions` | `session_id` |
| `POST` | `/v1/messages` | send; **edit** if `message_id` **and** `chat_id` set |
| `PATCH` / `POST /v1/messages/edit` | | `session_id`, `chat_id`, `message_id`, `content` |
| `DELETE` / `POST /v1/messages/delete` | | `session_id`, `chat_id?`, `message_id?`, `from?`, `delete_for_everyone?` |
| `POST` | `/v1/messages/read` | `session_id`, `chat_id`, `message_id` or `message_ids[]`, `from?` |
| `POST` | `/v1/chats` | `session_id`, `chat_id?`, `params?` → `{ ok, chat_id }` |
| `DELETE` | `/v1/chats` | `session_id`, `chat_id` |
| `POST` | `/v1/ingest` | Event JSON (`session_id` required, this credential) |
| `GET` | `/v1/media` | query `session_id`, `message_id` → bytes |

Send `params`: `username`, `phone_number`, `secret_chat`, `kind` (`image` `video` `file` `voice` `gif` `location` `contact`), `path`, **`data`** (standard base64 media bytes; Telegram), `filename`, `mime`, `lat`, `lng`, `name`, `phone`, `width`, `height`, `thumb_data`, `thumb_width`, `thumb_height`.

Telegram photos use `kind: "image"`. `data` is a **baseline JPEG** (not progressive, not mozjpeg). `width` and `height` are that JPEG’s pixel size; the gateway sets them on TDLib `inputPhoto`. `thumb_data` is a small baseline JPEG whose longest side is at most 320, with `thumb_width` and `thumb_height` matching that file. Secret chats show this thumbnail to the other party. Without it the chat preview and Telegram’s viewer stay blank, while saving the file and opening it in Photos can still look fine.

`GET /healthz` (no auth) → `{ "ok": true, "redis": "ok"|"down" }`. 401 media empty; 404 media empty; 429 `{ok:false}`.

